  "body": "## \ud83d\udc1b Bug\r\n\r\nConvolution weight gradient computation in nn.grad seems to be wrong when groups > 1.\r\n(conv1d_weight, conv2d_weight, conv3d_weight) \r\n\r\n## To Reproduce\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior: I attached my gist to print the difference between autograd and nn.grad.\r\nIn the script, I also suggest a correct alternative (only a minor change was sufficient)\r\n\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/lemonbuffer20/7c98cea1e904b2abaa38ce6d4ec9605e\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nnn.grad.convNd_weight should return the same result as F.conv2d backprop in groups > 1 case.\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\nPyTorch version: 1.7.1\r\nIs debug build: False\r\nCUDA used to build PyTorch: 10.1\r\nROCM used to build PyTorch: N/A\r\n\r\nOS: Ubuntu 20.04.1 LTS (x86_64)\r\nGCC version: (Ubuntu 9.3.0-17ubuntu1~20.04) 9.3.0\r\nClang version: Could not collect\r\nCMake version: version 3.16.3\r\n\r\nPython version: 3.7 (64-bit runtime)\r\nIs CUDA available: True\r\nCUDA runtime version: Could not collect\r\nGPU models and configuration: \r\nGPU 0: GeForce GTX TITAN X\r\n\r\nNvidia driver version: 460.32.03\r\ncuDNN version: Probably one of the following:\r\n/usr/local/cuda-11.0/targets/x86_64-linux/lib/libcudnn.so.8\r\n...\r\n\r\n## Additional context\r\n\r\n1.\r\nI believe the small difference (~=1e-6) of the result is inevitable.\r\nBut sometimes the max grad difference (both input and weight) goes to ~=1e-4, which seems much bigger.\r\nCan we remove, or at least reduce the error?\r\n\r\n2.\r\nIf you can verify my modification is correct, I'd be glad to propose PR.\n\ncc @ezyang @gchanan @zou3519 @albanD @gqchen @pearu @nikitaved @soulitzer @Lezcano @Varal7 @mruberry @jbschlosser @walterddr @kshitij12345 @bdhirsh",
